{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-1co-4-1","title":"1 Corinthians 4:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 In what account the ministers ought to be had. 7 We have nothing which we have not received. 9 The apostles spectacles to the world, angels, and men; 13 the filth and offscouring of the world; 15 yet our fathers in Christ; 16 whom we ought to follow.</p>\n<p>account. 13; 2Co 12:6 the ministers. 3:5; 9:16-18; Mt 24:45; 2Co 4:5; 6:4; 11:23; Col 1:25; 1Ti 3:6 and stewards. Lu 12:42; 16:1-3; Tit 1:7; 1Pe 4:10 mysteries. 2:7; Mt 13:11; Mr 4:11; Lu 8:10; Ro 16:25; Eph 1:9; 3:3-9; 6:19 Col 1:26,27; 2:2; 4:3; 1Ti 3:9,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-2","title":"1 Corinthians 4:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>that. 17; 7:25; Nu 12:7; Pr 13:17; Mt 25:21,23; Lu 12:42; 16:10-12 2Co 2:17; 4:2; Col 1:7; 4:7,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-3","title":"1 Corinthians 4:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>it is. 2:15; 1Sa 16:7; Joh 7:24 judgment. Gr. day. 3:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-4","title":"1 Corinthians 4:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>For.[Ouden gar emauto sunoida] \"For I am not conscious to myself of any guilt\" or neglect of duty. Wetstien has shown, from the classics, that this is the proper signification of [suneidein.]</p>\n<p>I know. Job 27:6; Ps 7:3-5; Joh 21:17; 2Co 1:12; 1Jo 3:20,21 yet. Job 9:2,3,20; 15:14; 25:4; 40:4; Ps 19:12; 130:3; 143:2; Pr 21:2 Ro 3:19,20; 4:2 but. 5; Ps 26:12; 50:6; 2Co 5:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-5","title":"1 Corinthians 4:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>judge. Mt 7:1,2; Lu 6:37; Ro 2:1,16; 14:4,10-13; Jas 4:11 until. 1:7; 11:26; 15:23; Mt 24:30,46; 1Th 5:2; Jas 5:7; 2Pe 3:4,12; Jude 1:14 Re 1:7 who. 3:13; Ec 11:9; 12:14; Mal 3:18; Lu 12:1-3; Ro 2:16; 2Co 4:2; Heb 4:13 Re 20:12 praise. Mt 25:21,23; Joh 5:44; Ro 2:7,29; 2Co 5:10; 10:18; 1Pe 1:7; 5:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-6","title":"1 Corinthians 4:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>these. 1:12; 3:4-7; 2Co 10:7,12,15; 11:4,12-15 for. 9:23; 2Co 4:15; 12:19; 1Th 1:5; 2Ti 2:10 that ye. Job 11:11,12; Ps 8:4; 146:3; Isa 2:22; Jer 17:5,6; Mt 23:8-10 Ro 12:3; 2Co 12:6 be puffed. 18,19; 3:21; 5:2,6; 8:1; 13:4; Nu 11:28,29; Joh 3:26,27; Col 2:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-7","title":"1 Corinthians 4:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>who. 12:4-11; 15:10; Ro 9:16-18; Eph 3:3-5; 2Th 2:12-14; 1Ti 1:12-15 Tit 3:3-7 maketh thee to differ. Gr. distinguisheth thee. and what. 3:5; 7:7; 1Ch 29:11-16; 2Ch 1:7-12; Pr 2:6; Mt 25:14,15; Lu 19:13 Joh 1:16; 3:27; Ro 1:5; 12:6; Jas 1:17; 1Pe 4:10 why. 5:6; 2Ch 32:23-29; Eze 28:2-5; 29:3; Da 4:30-32; 5:18,23 Ac 12:22,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-8","title":"1 Corinthians 4:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>ye are full. 1:5; 3:1,2; 5:6; Pr 13:7; 25:14; Isa 5:21; Lu 1:51-53; 6:25; Ro 12:3 Ro 12:16; Ga 6:3; Re 3:17 without. 18; Ac 20:29,30; Php 1:27; 2:12 and I. Nu 11:29; Ac 26:29; 2Co 11:1 ye did. Ps 122:5-9; Jer 28:6; Ro 12:15; 2Co 13:9; 1Th 2:19,20; 3:6-9 2Ti 2:11,12; Re 5:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-9","title":"1 Corinthians 4:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>I. 15:30-32; 2Co 1:8-10; 4:8-12; 6:9; Php 1:29,30; 1Th 3:3 us the apostles last, as. or, us the last apostles, as. Ps 44:22; Ro 8:36; 1Th 5:9,10; Re 6:9-11 we are. Heb 10:33; 11:36 spectacle. Gr. theatre. Ac 19:29,31 to angels, and to men. Heb 1:14; Re 7:11-14; 17:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-10","title":"1 Corinthians 4:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>are fools. 1:1-3,18-20,26-28; 2:3,14; 3:18; 2Ki 9:11; Ho 9:7; Ac 17:18,32 Ac 26:24 for. Mt 5:11; 10:22-25; 24:9; Lu 6:22; Ac 9:16; 1Pe 4:14 are wise. 8; 10:14,15; Jer 8:8,9 we are weak. 2:3; 2Co 10:10; 11:29; 12:9,10; 13:3,4,9 but ye. 3:2; 10:12 but we. Pr 11:12; Isa 53:3; Lu 10:16; 18:9; 1Th 4:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-11","title":"1 Corinthians 4:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>unto. 9:4; 2Co 4:8; 6:4,5; 11:26,27; Php 4:12 and are naked. Job 22:6; Ro 8:35 and are buffeted. Ac 14:19; 16:23; 23:2; 2Co 11:23-25; 2Ti 3:11 and have. Mt 8:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-12","title":"1 Corinthians 4:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>labour. 9:6; Ac 18:3; 20:34; 1Th 2:9; 2Th 3:8; 1Ti 4:10 being reviled. Mt 5:44; Lu 6:28; 23:34; Ac 7:60; Ro 12:14,20; 1Pe 2:23; 3:9; Jude 1:9 being persecuted. Mt 5:11; 1Pe 3:14; 4:12-14,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-13","title":"1 Corinthians 4:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>La 3:45; Ac 22:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-14","title":"1 Corinthians 4:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>write. 9:15; 2Co 7:3; 12:19 my. 15; 2Co 6:11-13; 11:11; 12:14,15; 1Th 2:11 I. Eze 3:21; Ac 20:31; Col 1:28; 1Th 5:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-15","title":"1 Corinthians 4:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>ye have. 2Ti 4:3 for. 3:6,10; 9:1,2; Ac 18:4-11; Ro 15:20; 2Co 3:1-3; Ga 4:19; Tit 1:4 Phm 1:10-12,19; Jas 1:18; 1Pe 1:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-16","title":"1 Corinthians 4:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>11:1; Joh 10:4,5; Php 3:17; 1Th 1:6; 2Th 3:9; Heb 13:7; 1Pe 5:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-17","title":"1 Corinthians 4:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>I sent. 16:10; Ac 19:21,22; Php 2:19; 1Th 3:2,3 who is. 15; 1Ti 1:2; 2Ti 1:2 faithful. 2; 7:25; Nu 12:7; Pr 13:17; Mt 24:45; 25:21,23; Eph 6:21; Col 1:7; 4:9 2Ti 2:2; Re 2:10,13 my ways. 7:17; 11:2,16; 16:1; 2Ti 3:10 in. 14:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-18","title":"1 Corinthians 4:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>6-8; 5:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-19","title":"1 Corinthians 4:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>I. 14:5; Ac 19:21; 2Co 1:15,17,23; 2:1,2 if. Ac 18:21; Ro 15:32; Heb 6:3; Jas 4:15 not. 18; 2Co 13:1-4 but. 2:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-20","title":"1 Corinthians 4:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>1:24; 2:4; Ro 1:16; 14:17; 15:19; 2Co 10:4,5; 1Th 1:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-4-21","title":"1 Corinthians 4:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>shall. 5:5; 2Co 10:2,6,8; 12:20,21; 13:2; 3:10 and. 2Co 10:1; 1Th 2:7; Jas 3:17</p>"}]}